hi,
the message indicates that he dont find /sbin/init. are you sure that
the root device is mounted ? (not mounted root devices cause also panic).
e.g if the driver for the scsi is not compiled in and the load in the
initrd fails, the root cant mounted.

If anything fails i would try to boot from a disk perhaps even use
busybox in a ramdisk.

	walter





